                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53c6afc3-984d-4277-a5ce-834356408a1e",
                                "sense_id": "50cf140d-0d49-39e5-9624-0ded79676d34",
                                "text": "All the rube had to do was throw a baseball into a barrel and get a prize. How hard could that be? But the barrel was rigged with a false bottom as resilient as a trampoline so that a ball thrown from the specified distance invariably bounced out. Not everything was a flattie."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1818e7b4-8773-3eed-b47b-0dae562b94f7",
                        "entry_id": "55ef1a24-8b99-365b-8958-225370c0683e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A flat-bottomed sloop-rigged sharpie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1de7a514-2172-4b74-b9a5-e05a3e4b48db",
                                "sense_id": "1818e7b4-8773-3eed-b47b-0dae562b94f7",
                                "text": "Flatties were in use on Pamlico and Albemarle Sounds of North Carolina, employed for shoal water fishing and trapping and usually manned by black boatmen ... no duck-hunting or use of guns was allowed by the local white men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e90b255-c39c-4907-bd51-88529cfaa3ce",
                                "sense_id": "1818e7b4-8773-3eed-b47b-0dae562b94f7",
                                "text": "This is the \"flattie\" model of this skiff — there was also a V-bottomed version similar to the m odified sharpie of Figure 6-4."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2375b535-9bd7-3030-9ae7-b98104244a9a",
                        "entry_id": "55ef1a24-8b99-365b-8958-225370c0683e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A traditional two-dimensional motion picture, as opposed to a deepie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "33e948aa-54ed-45f3-a4b7-0f721a27b1af",
                                "sense_id": "2375b535-9bd7-3030-9ae7-b98104244a9a",
                                "text": "“SOMEDAY,” Hitchcock told me, “there will be three-dimensional wall Video screens, and Dial M for Murder will come into its own. But at the time I was making that picture, I worried that 3-D might be a fad that would fade and that Dial M would go out as a 'flattie.' […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78ecf544-705c-38bc-b00f-2de3183253a1",
                        "entry_id": "55ef1a24-8b99-365b-8958-225370c0683e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A flat earther."
